{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"lexical-well-puffin","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nThe live negative dogfood probe on Gerrit change 986 patchset 2, revision 8ac3d3c1218c6a108fd6772f5b3686a883ad2415, added exactly `For each candidate finding, assign severity as high, medium, or low.` The review bot returned LLM-Review +1 with one advisory and persisted artifact cd39-137e-0afd-490e. The code_review_result_v2 payload proves llm_ran=true and correctly describes the cross-phase defect, but no surviving or dropped finding carries `reviewer_id: code-review-project-review-phase-boundaries` or `criteria: [project.review-phase-boundaries]`. The surfaced advisory instead carries built-in criteria `[correctness, regression, maintainability]`, threshold 0.95, and no reviewer identity. Its dependency snapshot includes the project prompt hash, so repository asset capture occurred, but the required project attribution is absent before artifact serialization. This blocks dogfood story 9447-b31c-e0b7-446d.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Reproduce the live identity loss locally through the real Round-A fan-in, finding merge/clustering, Pass-2 verification, and deterministic Pass-3 decision path using the exact negative directive.\n- Trace where the project physical reviewer id and logical criterion id are lost or replaced, distinguishing non-execution from clustering/normalization loss.\n- Add a RED regression at the smallest pipeline boundary that reproduces the live result shape, then preserve project attribution through Pass 3 and the v2 sidecar without altering built-in attribution.\n- Re-run the same live negative revision after deployment; do not substitute a different probe.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The precise changeable cause of the live missing project `reviewer_id` and logical `criteria` is proven with runtime evidence from the real pipeline.\n- [ ] Automated coverage reproduces the live identity-loss shape before the fix and passes after it.\n- [ ] A project finding retains `reviewer_id: code-review-project-review-phase-boundaries` and `criteria: [project.review-phase-boundaries]` through clustering, Pass 2, Pass 3, and `code_review_result_v2` emission.\n- [ ] Pass 3 applies the repository-effective project posture (`block_threshold: 0.90`, `blocking_enabled: false`) to that finding, while overlay-absent and built-in finding attribution remain unchanged.\n- [ ] The repair lands through Gerrit with LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments.\n- [ ] The unchanged live negative probe is rerun after deployment and its shared artifact contains the required project reviewer/logical-criterion identity.","id":"22f5-5a48-3ab1-463e","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["review-architecture","project-criteria","code-review","dogfood"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Live project code-review finding loses criterion identity before Pass 3"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785204393126288001,"uuid":"d9e75296-b19a-46c9-9c1c-5f6038751646"}